{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1526039-a-sin-eater-enter-wod-how-would-they-stereotype-wod-splat-and-mortal-and-vice-versa","id":1526039,"title":"A Sin-Eater enter WoD how would they stereotype WoD splat and mortal, and vice-versa?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-27T23:48:53-08:00","id":1526039,"title":"A Sin-Eater enter WoD how would they stereotype WoD splat and mortal, and vice-versa?","content":"I'm thinking of a possible crossover between CofD and WoD, I own the 20th aniversary for WoD, and everything for Chronicle of Darkness, so I wanted to know how Sin-Eater would interact with WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T01:37:12-08:00","id":1526043,"title":"","content":"Which Sin-Eater? There's a lot to consider - their Burden, their Krewe Archetype (and for that matter, whether they're together with their krewe or not), the nature of their Geist, and so on. So much personal aspects to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T03:50:47-08:00","id":1526047,"title":"","content":"Mostly the same as they would in Chronicles. You will have to adjust a few things, like wraiths needing help, and figure out ways for Sin Eaters to enter the realms of the dead and things like that but ultimately the way the sin eaters themselves act won't change. <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T07:20:30-08:00","id":1526064,"title":"","content":"While the underlying motivations of Sin-Eaters won't change, the Wraith Underworld will present them with dilemmas that Ghost Underworld doesn't. The sprawling Hierarchy with all its Guilds and Legions contains politics which are more complex than anything Sin-Eaters are used to. The existence of Oblivion and its Spectres will force them to decide whether helping Wraiths pass on is the responsible thing to do, when every pair of hands is needed for the war. Will they see Spectres as in need of help, an invader to be destroyed, resources, or as lost causes? Ghosts they knew didn't have Shadows either, so the way Wraiths function will take some getting used to.<br /> <br /> In the other direction, Sin-Eaters are unlike anything the Hierarchy is used to. Dead but alive, with something Spectre-like-but-not-really riding shotgun. Laws of the Hierarchy and experiences of individual Wraiths couldn't have accounted for them. Expect a lot of panicking and scheming when Wraiths decide how to respond.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that Sin-Eaters are tied to the Underworld, but not <i>this</i> Underworld. Trying to interact with the new one with their Haunts, Ceremonies and default powers may be like trying to run a Windows program in Linux. Do they work as intended, fail utterly or do they come with weird glitches and caveats? Are Catabasis and Cabeiros possible? Is resurrection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T15:50:42-08:00","id":1526088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1526039-a-sin-eater-enter-wod-how-would-they-stereotype-wod-splat-and-mortal-and-vice-versa?p=1526064#post1526064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the underlying motivations of Sin-Eaters won't change, the Wraith Underworld will present them with dilemmas that Ghost Underworld doesn't. The sprawling Hierarchy with all its Guilds and Legions contains politics which are more complex than anything Sin-Eaters are used to. The existence of Oblivion and its Spectres will force them to decide whether helping Wraiths pass on is the responsible thing to do, when every pair of hands is needed for the war. Will they see Spectres as in need of help, an invader to be destroyed, resources, or as lost causes? Ghosts they knew didn't have Shadows either, so the way Wraiths function will take some getting used to.<br /> <br /> In the other direction, Sin-Eaters are unlike anything the Hierarchy is used to. Dead but alive, with something Spectre-like-but-not-really riding shotgun. Laws of the Hierarchy and experiences of individual Wraiths couldn't have accounted for them. Expect a lot of panicking and scheming when Wraiths decide how to respond.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that Sin-Eaters are tied to the Underworld, but not <i>this</i> Underworld. Trying to interact with the new one with their Haunts, Ceremonies and default powers may be like trying to run a Windows program in Linux. Do they work as intended, fail utterly or do they come with weird glitches and caveats? Are Catabasis and Cabeiros possible? Is resurrection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great respond.<br /> I think when they use their power, they open a tiny dimensional rift, so that they power could still work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T18:59:36-08:00","id":1526099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1526039-a-sin-eater-enter-wod-how-would-they-stereotype-wod-splat-and-mortal-and-vice-versa?p=1526088#post1526088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great respond.<br /> I think when they use their power, they open a tiny dimensional rift, so that they power could still work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could actually combine this with the idea of the CoD Underworld changing the WoD Underworld, with the necrotic Essence flowing through the rifts. Maybe while typical uses of the Haunts have the rifts close after use, using Keys, which are more tied to the CoD Ghosts, could cause them to last longer, remain open, allow more Essence to come through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T00:13:21-08:00","id":1526105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1526039-a-sin-eater-enter-wod-how-would-they-stereotype-wod-splat-and-mortal-and-vice-versa?p=1526099#post1526099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could actually combine this with the idea of the CoD Underworld changing the WoD Underworld, with the necrotic Essence flowing through the rifts. Maybe while typical uses of the Haunts have the rifts close after use, using Keys, which are more tied to the CoD Ghosts, could cause them to last longer, remain open, allow more Essence to come through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank for the idea, but how would the Ghostly Essence of CofD affect WoD Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T19:27:06-08:00","id":1531490,"title":"","content":"Like has been said before, it really depends on the Burden and the Krewe Archetype, but I personally tied werewolves and sin-eaters together as sort of two sides of a liminal coin in my chronicles back in nWoD. For cWoD.. I don't think Geist really fits in with the cosmology much at all. Sin-Eaters would be enemies of the Hierarchy from day 1 and would be hunted down with extreme prejudice. With their Liminal Aura especially, you'd have so many Guilds gunning to either destroy or capture sin-eaters to figure out how they work so they could either monopolize this ability or learn to incorporate it into their Arcanoi. Garou would see them as nothing more than some sort of bizarre Fomori that need to be exterminated, the Technocracy would see them as major Reality Deviants thanks to how their presence messes with the Shroud and plays havoc with Consensus.. and the various Necromantic Clans and Bloodlines would see the Bound as either a rival competitor over access to ghosts or a potential resource to exploit..<br /> <br /> I don't really see sin-eaters doing particularly well in the classic World of Darkness, its much more overtly hostile splat wise in the old setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T13:08:17-08:00","id":1557558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1526039-a-sin-eater-enter-wod-how-would-they-stereotype-wod-splat-and-mortal-and-vice-versa#post1526039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of a possible crossover between CofD and WoD, I own the 20th aniversary for WoD, and everything for Chronicle of Darkness, so I wanted to know how Sin-Eater would interact with WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they are going to hate the Giovanni if they ever run into them. Depends on the numbers though. One Krewe is just not big enough to fight an entire clan. All sin-eaters being in owod mean the Giovanni probably never sleep well again. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}